# Ubergraph .gitignore.example
#
# The shipped .gitignore keeps the base clean: it publishes the manager (bridge/, tools/, docs/, profile examples, the authoring
# project's plugin source) and ignores everything that belongs to one game (analysis/, mods/, local profiles).
#
# To version YOUR mods and analysis inside your own copy of the base, copy this file over .gitignore. It drops the two game-specific
# ignores and keeps every safety rule: no game assets, no extractions, no mapping files, no local paths, no secrets.
*.exe
*.dll
*.pak
*.utoc
*.ucas
*.uasset
*.uexp
*.ubulk
*.dmp
*.log
*.ghidra
*.gpr
*.rep
node_modules/

# Local-only profile paths and credentials/configuration
**/games.local.json
.env
.env.*
profiles/*.local.json
/config/*.local.*

# Local catalogs, SQLite sidecars, and generated build output
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-*
*.db
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/.vs/

# Mapping files are derived from the game and stay local
*.usmap
*.jmap

# Full local IoStore extractions of proprietary game content; never publish
analysis/iostore-extract-*/
*.umap
*.uptnl
*.ushaderbytecode

# Unreal authoring project: track only the uproject, Config, Source and plugin source (assets are generated by scripts)
unreal/**/Content/
unreal/**/Intermediate/
unreal/**/Binaries/
unreal/**/Saved/
unreal/**/DerivedDataCache/
unreal/**/.vs/
unreal/**/*.sln
unreal/**/*.slnx
unreal/**/Config/DefaultEditorPerProjectUserSettings.ini
unreal/**/Config/DefaultInput.ini
unreal/**/Config/User*.ini

# Generated stand-ins for the game classes (derived from the usmap): local only
unreal/**/Plugins/*Stubs/

tools/bpdump/bin/
tools/bpdump/obj/

# Python bytecode caches
__pycache__/
*.pyc
